-> `loop <var> over <array> get <result>` is the only iteration form —
-> no `while`, no counters, no recursion. A loop runs exactly as many times
-> as the array is long, known before it starts, so a program's total work
-> is always statically bounded.
prices = [12, 45, 8, 99, 3, 61]

loop p over prices get affordable {
    if p < 50 {
        yield p
    }
}

-> `yield` collects values into the named result — here, a filtered array.
assert affordable = [12, 45, 8, 3]
